SUMMARY:Robert Junker Seminar: Mechanisms underlying ecological stability
DESCRIPTION:Prof. Dr. Robert R. Junker will give an online seminar titled "Mechanisms underlying ecological stability".\n\nGlobal change drivers restructure communities\, are major drivers of biodiversity decline\, and thus destabilize ecosystems. Nonetheless\, some individuals\, species\, and communities better tolerate environmental stresses than others suggesting specific mechanisms increasing their resilience and resistance. In my talk I will explore ecological processes underlying ecosystem stability and plant tolerance: 1) Response diversity\, which is the ability of some species to compensate for the loss of others due to different responses to environmental changes\, has been identified as an important but understudied component of biodiversity that facilitates ecosystem stability. 2) Universal trait spaces that may help to align responses to global change drivers across taxa. Understanding these mechanisms will help to inform conservation efforts protecting natural or restoring degraded ecosystems.\n\nZoom: https://uzh.zoom.us/j/64390599791?pwd=MoADAJz6dJRRmHEu1pRdnxpMQPozU9.1
LOCATION:Zoom
